Local changes since the fork:
- SKILL.md addresses the scripts by absolute path, so the documented commands
  work from any cwd. Keep the process cwd at the target project: the scaffold
  derives the project from cwd by design.
- validate_handoff.py decides READY/BLOCKED from concrete blockers (secrets,
  remaining TODOs, missing required sections). The upstream 0-100 quality
  score was removed: it scored heading presence, so a handoff full of
  unfilled TODOs still cleared its 70 threshold.
- validate_handoff.py no longer reports an already-redacted value as a leaked
  secret (`PASSWORD="..."` blocked a real handoff), and resolves cited paths
  by walking up to the directory holding .claude/ instead of assuming a fixed
  depth. Re-run over 28 stored handoffs: 26 READY, 2 blocked, both correctly
  (they are runbooks kept in the handoffs directory, not handoffs).
- Slimmed to what is actually used, measured over 28 handoffs in local
  transcripts: create_handoff 31 invocations, validate_handoff 102,
  list_handoffs 3, check_staleness 1. Dropped list_handoffs.py,
  check_staleness.py (both replaced by two shell one-liners in SKILL.md),
  references/resume-checklist.md (inlined), README.md, and evals/.

